So I finally ascended Wiz the wizard (original, huh?), who had the 
stingy dungeon without +Magic Missile (also without +Clairvoyance, 
+Protection, and +Cone of Cold until Vlad's Tower, so it's not as if 
Magic Missile should feel special in its lack of random generation).

The early game was standard; Mines' End was the version with the 
spellbooks, and Sokoban was with the bag of holding. Any source of 
reflection was noticeably absent through the mid-game. My big early 
find was a +4 orcish helm, which I wore until my final preparations for 
Rodney. 

I went to Ludios in search of a silver dragon for reflection (plus for 
experience enough to get me into the quest). A black dragon there 
disintegrated my original CoMR and my studded leather armor before I 
realized that wands of death do work on dragons, and that a black 
dragon up against a character without reflection is a very worthy time 
to use the wand. Dead dragons, scroll, shiny new reflective armor, +RC 
on a bones file [CoMR to replace the lost. 

Somewhere in here [Speed boots showed up, and a soldier donated +3 
leather gloves and something or other gave me the experience for the 
quest.

The quest, as per usual for wizards, was the quest. 

Somewhere in here, after the quest, I danced with some incubi which 
were generated while I was kicking sinks in hopes of a ring of 
levitation. By the time I reached the Castle I was XL 21 or so but I 
still had no ring. (I used +Levitation instead.)

After doing the Castle and the VoD, I hung around what seemed like 
forever, sacrificing in hopes of finally getting the Magic Missile 
spellbook. Finally I wrote the thing myself, and +Magic Mapping and 
+Detect Treasure while I was at it. (Markers came from, IIRC, a bones 
file and a random generation in the mines. There would be another 
randomly generated marker, in Gehennom, later.)

Gehennom went fast and clean.

All this was, incidentally, with the +0 MB as my weapon. Thoth granted 
me nothing else of value, and I was focusing on praying for spellbooks 
rather than waiting for gifts. I enchanted a pile of elven daggers but 
never actually got around to throwing them.

After my final preparations my AC was -34 or so, which is not ideal for 
me but I decided against wishing up a tee shirt because I had tons of 
assorted healing potions to alchemize and I already was XL 30 with 
something like 300 hit points. Once again, and it's the "once again" 
part that kills me, I learned that combining !Extra Healing with !Gain 
Ability does not, in fact, create !Full Healing. OTOH, I had 58 potions 
of water suddenly available, so blessing everything in sight was easy.

Right about then I realized that I hadn't gotten teleportitis yet and 
that I'd probably want it for Gehennom on the way back up. A few 
thousand turns of Create Monster and searching the dungeon and a cursed 
scroll of Genocide produced not one corpse of a tengu, nymph, or 
leprechaun. Finally I gave up on waiting-- which it seemed like I'd 
done a lot of (both the waiting and the giving up on waiting) in this 
dungeon.

For the first time, I managed my inventory well and wasn't close to 
burdened for the final run. Also for the first time, I tried the Haste 
Self-jumping boots combination for the final run. I don't love the 
interface/gameplay aspect of jumping, but for the final run back up I 
can deal with the clunky interface issue.

Rodney came back three times early (like 300 turns between one death 
and the next) then not again until Earth. The Force got me maybe four 
or five times, nothing terrible.

I stopped at my stash one last time on the way up and realized that + 
Magic Missile would likely expire before the game would end (but wasn't 
so old as to be renewable just yet). So for the first time I brought 
heavy reading material along for the planes.

Also I enchanted MB to +3, as if the +3 would make any difference 
against what I'd be in melee with on Astral.

On Earth, I read my first (of four that I brought) ?Gold Detection 
while stunned rather than confused. Oops. It took me a long time on 
Water to realize that I had tons of marker charges remaining and some 
blank scrolls that really, I wouldn't be stopping to write on Astral. 
So.

On Astral, I landed toward the right, which was Death and a chaotic 
altar. Death took abour 30 HP from my max.

In the middle was Pesty, and the neutral altar.

I sacrificed and nice things happened.

Final stats: St:18/99 Dx:18 Co:18 In:18 Wi:18 Ch:16. HP:156(337) Pw:220
(505) AC:-34 Exp:30 T:61181.

This wasn't the first time I've done a wish/geno/poly/polyselfless 
ascension, but it was significantly cleaner and easier than it had been 
before. Had I not been hanging around for Magic Missile (and then for 
teleportitis), I'd have been done at around 50K turns, which was my 
goal coming into the game. 

Onward.

